+# PAL Host Menu SC (bounded OFL font subset)
+
+This directory contains a small modified Noto Sans CJK SC font subset for the host menu only. It is not a full Chinese font and contains no game assets or fonts extracted from a game. The game renderer and advanced ImGui launcher are unchanged.
+
+## Source and license
+
+- Upstream: https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk
+- Upstream font license: https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk/blob/main/Sans/LICENSE
+- Installed input: `/usr/share/fonts/opentype/noto/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc` and `NotoSansCJK-Bold.ttc`, Simplified Chinese face index **2**, version **2.004**.
+- The source font's own copyright record is **© 2014-2021 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/).** The installed distribution's copyright notice also lists **2010-2012 Google Corporation**. Both notices accompany the output in `LICENSE.txt`.
+- Source SHA-256 hashes, exact original version strings, output hashes and the full Unicode repertoire are in `manifest.json`.
+- License: **SIL Open Font License 1.1**. The OFL expressly allows modifying and embedding font software and defines deletion of components as a modified version. Retain the copyright notice and license, distribute the font under OFL, do not sell the font by itself, and do not use reserved font names for a derivative without permission.
+- This derivative is renamed **PAL Host Menu SC**, with PostScript names `PALHostMenuSC-Regular` and `PALHostMenuSC-Bold`. All primary name records and CFF font/FD names are renamed; source copyright and trademark notices remain attribution only. No endorsement is implied.
+- The complete license and notices are provided in `LICENSE.txt` **and embedded in each font's readable OpenType name-ID 13 metadata**, so compiled-in copies retain the text. Include this directory's license in source/package notices as well.
+
+The full installed TTCs are not shipped. `pal_menu_cjk_regular.h` and `pal_menu_cjk_bold.h` are readable byte arrays holding the small CFF/OpenType subsets. The font bytes remain OFL-licensed regardless of the surrounding application's license.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+The audited environment already had Python and **fontTools 4.61.1**. No package or font download was used. From the project root, with the two matching locally installed source files:
+
+    python3 runtime/third_party/pal-menu-cjk/generate.py --source-dir /usr/share/fonts/opentype/noto
+
+The source font hashes must match `manifest.json` to reproduce the exact committed output. Generation is deterministic with these sources, the current `LICENSE.txt` and `host_menu_text.h`, and the documented fontTools version. The script selects face 2, subsets only the non-ASCII characters of the host label string literals, removes unused layout/vertical tables, preserves source copyright metadata, renames the derivative, embeds the complete OFL, and emits the byte headers, `glyphs.h`, and manifest. It refuses empty or unexpectedly large repertoires and missing source glyphs.
+
+When adding a new Chinese host label, add it to `src/host/host_menu_text.h`, regenerate these files, and rerun the font and text-bounds tests. `ui.cpp` still uses the existing Inter fonts for ASCII, digits, `%`, Saturn button letters and existing special symbols. It uses these subsets only for exact matched codepoints and draws unsupported codepoints as Inter `?`. Atlas growth is capped; normal runtime builds require neither Python/fontTools nor external font files.
+
+Harmony (`PAL_OHOS_DEFAULTS` or `__OHOS__`) defaults to the Chinese host labels. Desktop builds remain English. An explicit compiler definition `PAL_HOST_MENU_CHINESE=0` or `=1` overrides the default without altering settings keys or game text. Existing labels and the layout editor's anticipated labels are centralized in the helper; an editor integration must still connect the relevant enum values to its drawing code.
